Z||000000||85fierogt||09-17-2001||05:27 PM||||ok guys I have an 85 fiero gt 4 speed manual 2.8 v6 with a  Centerforce clutch and every time I throw it up to reverse it doesn't let me it just make a grinding noise and I really hate to push that in fear that something just isn't right here, any ideas?1?!?!<BR>peace<BR>-brad<BR>P.S all the other gears operate flawlessly <p>[This message has been edited by 85fierogt (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||09-17-2001||06:22 PM||||Before putting it into reverse, drop it into another gear like 2nd and then into reverse while the clutch is disengaged.  No double clutching.  That'll only get those gears spinning again.  Putting it into 2nd should stop the gears from spinning enough to make a nice quiet shift into reverse.  <BR>If your gears still grind after getting that technique done properly, I would think your clutch isn't disengaging all the way.  Bleeding the system might help.  <P>How much pressure does your pressure plate apply?  Do you know if you clutch fork is up for the job of disengaging that clutch?  I found out the expensive F!!$$*&@%&^$ way and went back to a stock clutch and new clutch fork, which should have been replaced the first time through.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||85fierogt||09-17-2001||06:32 PM||||i dont really know the answers to any of those questions because i just bought the car like 2 months ago, and i tried your technique it helped a little bit but what im wondering here is why it makes that noise even in idle ?!?!? thats what got me?<BR>peace<BR>-brad||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||09-17-2001||06:42 PM||||I have an 84.  I know its a 4cyl but I still have a similar problem.  I have a 4 speed so it might be different as well there too.  When I move it to the left to go to reverse, it will be fine, but if I try to push it up quick, it will grind.  If I keep it there, you can hear the grind gradually get slower, until it stops.  Rather than keep it there grinding however, I just pull it to the right and wait a second for it to wind down before I push it up and into gear.  It usually takes about 3 to 4 seconds.  I think the short wait of holding it to the left before pushing it up is worth not grinding the gear.  This is Just my situation, maybe you can push it to the right, hold for a sec. then try pulling down to R.  I don't know, just my little life story. =)||||reg||1
